# ---- Generated artefacts ----
# The FAISS index, parent store and Docling cache ARE committed on purpose, so
# the project is plug-and-play: clone, set .env, run, ask a question. Rebuilding
# them means a multi-minute Docling parse plus re-embedding, which is a poor
# first impression for a reviewer.
#
# The caveat: a FAISS index is tied to the embedding model that built it. The
# committed one is all-MiniLM-L6-v2. Changing EMBEDDING_MODEL requires
# re-running `python scripts/ingest_cli.py --reset`, or query and stored vectors
# will come from different models and retrieval will quietly return nonsense.
#
# Uploads and job records stay out: uploads duplicate files committed
# elsewhere, and job records are per-run state with no value to a reader.
data/uploads/
data/jobs/
data/*.json
data/*.pkl
*.log
logs/

# ---- ML model caches ----
.hf_cache/
models/
*.bin
*.safetensors

